; force per unit area inside a material. σ = F/A. unit: pascal (Pa).
; the internal force that a material develops to resist external load.
; three types:
; normal stress: force perpendicular to cross-section (compression or tension).
; shear stress: force parallel to cross-section (sliding).
; bearing stress: stress at a contact point.
; 
; the fundamental civil engineering quantity.
; a bridge must not be stressed beyond its yield strength.
; design: σ_working = σ_ultimate / safety_factor.
; 
; stress and pressure are dimensionally identical (Pa = N/m²).
; difference: pressure is isotropic (same in all directions) — fluid.
; stress is directional — solid material.

(kosha stress
  (vishesa civil-varga engineering-varga)
  (swarupa subanta)
  (yukta force area strain young-modulus yield-strength safety-factor)
  (abheda pressure))
